From: meta-st-odyssey <build@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] configs: stm32mp15: enable Micrel KSZ90x1 PHY driver

Neither CONFIG_PHY_MICREL nor CONFIG_PHY_GENERIC is set in this
defconfig, so the KSZ9031RN on the Seeed Odyssey-STM32MP157C ends up
bound to U-Boot's generic ethernet PHY driver (confirmed via
"dm tree": eth_phy_generic_drv, not a Micrel one). The generic driver
only does bare IEEE-standard register access and skips whatever
vendor-specific KSZ9031 setup this PHY needs - with it, autonegotiation
never completes ("Waiting for PHY auto negotiation to complete...
TIMEOUT!") even after the DMA_MODE_SWR / st,eth-clk-sel fix in this
same layer got the MAC itself talking to the PHY correctly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [out-of-tree board defconfig change -
this defconfig is shared by every ST stm32mp15 board, but enabling a
PHY driver that only activates for boards whose devicetree PHY ID
actually matches a KSZ9021/KSZ9031 is harmless for the others]

--- a/configs/stm32mp15_defconfig
+++ b/configs/stm32mp15_defconfig
@@ -188,3 +188,5 @@
 CONFIG_FWU_MDATA_V2=y
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_MKFWUMDATA is not set
+CONFIG_PHY_MICREL=y
+CONFIG_PHY_MICREL_KSZ90X1=y
